From: QEMU Anti-Detection Patches
Date: 2025
Subject: [PATCH] target/i386: Hide KVM hypervisor presence when expose_kvm is disabled

When the user sets "-cpu host,-kvm" (expose_kvm=false), also clear the
CPUID[1].ECX[31] hypervisor bit and suppress all Hyper-V CPUID leaves
at 0x40000000.

The original code only cleared FEAT_KVM; the hypervisor bit in FEAT_1_ECX
was left set from the unconditional set in x86_cpu_load_model() or from
the host passthrough feature expansion.  Additionally, if hv-* flags were
enabled, hyperv_fill_cpuids() would still populate the 0x40000000 Hyper-V
CPUID leaves with the configured hv-vendor-id.

Without this patch, even with "-cpu host,-kvm,-hypervisor" and hv-* flags,
the 0x40000000 leaf range can still be discovered by the guest.

Bugfix: simply guarding hyperv_init_vcpu() in kvm_arch_init_vcpu() with
an !expose_kvm check caused an abort: the MSR setup in kvm_put_msrs()
would still try to write Hyper-V MSRs (e.g. HV_X64_MSR_SVERSION at
0x40000081) because cpu->hyperv_features was not cleared.  KVM would
reject these writes since SynIC was never enabled, triggering an
assertion failure.

The fix clears cpu->hyperv_features alongside FEAT_KVM so that the
entire Hyper-V code path is disabled consistently: hyperv_enabled()
returns false, hyperv_init_vcpu() is never called, and kvm_put_msrs()
skips all Hyper-V MSRs.

---
 target/i386/cpu.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/target/i386/cpu.c b/target/i386/cpu.c
index abcdef1..1234567 100644
--- a/target/i386/cpu.c
+++ b/target/i386/cpu.c
@@ -9613,6 +9613,17 @@
 
     if (!kvm_enabled() || !cpu->expose_kvm) {
         env->features[FEAT_KVM] = 0;
+        env->features[FEAT_1_ECX] &= ~CPUID_EXT_HYPERVISOR;
+
+        /*
+         * Clear all Hyper-V feature bits so that hyperv_enabled() returns
+         * false, preventing hyperv_init_vcpu() from being called and,
+         * most importantly, preventing kvm_put_msrs() from adding Hyper-V
+         * MSRs (e.g. HV_X64_MSR_SVERSION = 0x40000081) to the KVM MSR set.
+         */
+        cpu->hyperv_features = 0;
+        cpu->hyperv_passthrough = false;
+        cpu->hyperv_spinlock_attempts = HYPERV_SPINLOCK_NEVER_NOTIFY;
     }
 
     /*
